WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.380
A gallery.

2
00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.620
A duke draws back a
curtain for his visitor:

3
00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:10.250
"That's my last Duchess painted on the
wall," His voice stays calm and courteous.

4
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.540
Yet somewhere in his words is a crime.

5
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:18.060
Elsewhere, an old sailor stops a
wedding guest outside the feast.

6
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.890
"He holds him with his glittering eye".

7
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.090
A murderer speaks, and we listen calmly.

8
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.730
So what is the poem making us do?

9
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.660
In this mission, you'll
meet the dramatic monologue:

10
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.940
one speaker, and a
listener who never speaks.

11
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:36.100
You'll ask what the speaker
isn't telling his visitor.

12
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.200
And you'll meet a listener who
can't leave until the tale is told.

13
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.740
Your mission: work out
what the poem makes us do.
